{
  "case_id": "2010-09-804",
  "document_hash": "f38a7621a5795b00ac20400d6f5045f6f069881bcca71d1e8ead0beed0e85dca",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2010-09-804",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f38a7621a5795b00ac20400d6f5045f6f069881bcca71d1e8ead0beed0e85dca",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f38a7621a579-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Tuesday, November 30, 2010"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2010-09-804",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f38a7621a5795b00ac20400d6f5045f6f069881bcca71d1e8ead0beed0e85dca",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f38a7621a579-0000-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Congress crafted a carefully balanced ERISA enforcement scheme that enables plan participants to recover plan benefits under section 502(a)(1)(B) and equitable remedies for ERISA violations under section 502(a)(3)."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2010-09-804",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f38a7621a5795b00ac20400d6f5045f6f069881bcca71d1e8ead0beed0e85dca",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f38a7621a579-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: Mr. Olson, when you say the employees had no choice, but the district court found, didn't it, that the reason for this plan summary being misleading was that the employer, Cigna, feared that there might be a backlash on the part of the employees if they found out, if they were told the truth about this plan; that is, that it was less favorable, that they would not have the same benefits that they had under the prior plan?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2010-09-804",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f38a7621a5795b00ac20400d6f5045f6f069881bcca71d1e8ead0beed0e85dca",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f38a7621a579-0000-0004",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 19,
        "start": 19
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the record suggests in various parts -- I can't remember exactly which page to refer to -- that $70 million would be the consequence of this against the plan, on which some people, depending upon how long they were with the company, when they left the company, whether they were about to retire, whether they stayed longer and the interest rates fluctuated, there can be all --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondents",
      "case_id": "2010-09-804",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "f38a7621a5795b00ac20400d6f5045f6f069881bcca71d1e8ead0beed0e85dca",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f38a7621a579-0001-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The petition -- the Respondents in this case, the named members of the class, claim that they were out 30-some thousand dollars each."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Olson",
      "case_id": "2010-09-804",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "f38a7621a5795b00ac20400d6f5045f6f069881bcca71d1e8ead0beed0e85dca",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f38a7621a579-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Mr. Olson: Well, Chief Justice -- Mr. Chief Justice, that is the statute. The statute gives you relief with respect to a misleading plan summary under the laws of equity."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Olson",
      "case_id": "2010-09-804",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "f38a7621a5795b00ac20400d6f5045f6f069881bcca71d1e8ead0beed0e85dca",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f38a7621a579-0001-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Mr. Olson: Yes, well, the Second Circuit suggested, and the Government and Respondents, particularly the Respondents, say if there's a material difference, likely harm is presumed."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2010-09-804",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "f38a7621a5795b00ac20400d6f5045f6f069881bcca71d1e8ead0beed0e85dca",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f38a7621a579-0001-0008",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 34,
        "start": 34
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Justice Breyer: What happens in a trust law where, let's say, there are 10 or 50,000 beneficiaries in a trust, and -- and the trustee has indeed made an error."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Cigna",
      "case_id": "2010-09-804",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f38a7621a5795b00ac20400d6f5045f6f069881bcca71d1e8ead0beed0e85dca",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f38a7621a579-0002-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "that there was a real prospect of employee backlash if the employees knew about these benefit reductions. It's well-established in behavioral economics that people are very averse to losses. So if a -- if the statute and the regulations are requiring the loss to be disclosed, it isn't going out on a limb to say that there's going to be a reaction to that. And here, Cigna knew that there was a reaction to that, and they had examples from the press of with Deloitte & Touche had had a similar situation where they had to roll back the cash balance changes because employees were so upset."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2010-09-804",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f38a7621a5795b00ac20400d6f5045f6f069881bcca71d1e8ead0beed0e85dca",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f38a7621a579-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: Under your proposal, I assume, if you prevail, under your position, the -- the summaries will now become part of the plan."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2010-09-804",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f38a7621a5795b00ac20400d6f5045f6f069881bcca71d1e8ead0beed0e85dca",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f38a7621a579-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: If an administrator -- if an administrator issues a summary plan description that is 100 pages long and is basically the same thing as the written instrument, and that's a violation of the requirement in ERISA that it be a summary and that it be intelligible to ordinary readers, what remedy is available to a beneficiary?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Bruce",
      "case_id": "2010-09-804",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f38a7621a5795b00ac20400d6f5045f6f069881bcca71d1e8ead0beed0e85dca",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f38a7621a579-0002-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. BRUCE: Well, as we said in the brief, there are already cases that -- that recognize exceptions to liability here, and one of them is for prompt correction of any problem. So if you have the unintentional error in that unintentionally the wear-away provisions weren't disclosed, well, then the issue is: Why wasn't that corrected at any point in time? We're now 12 years out, and Cigna has never disclosed those wear-aways to anyone."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Bruce",
      "case_id": "2010-09-804",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f38a7621a5795b00ac20400d6f5045f6f069881bcca71d1e8ead0beed0e85dca",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f38a7621a579-0002-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. BRUCE: Well, intentional errors should not be countenanced, and here Cigna was deliberately misleading employees. If it's an unintentional error, then it should be promptly corrected."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States (amicus)",
      "case_id": "2010-09-804",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f38a7621a5795b00ac20400d6f5045f6f069881bcca71d1e8ead0beed0e85dca",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f38a7621a579-0002-0006",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 41,
        "start": 41
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "ON BEHALF OF THE UNITED STATES, AS AMICUS CURIAE, SUPPORTING RESPONDENTS MR. KNEEDLER: Mr. Chief Justice, and may it please the Court: The pension benefits an employee accrues while she works are a major component of her compensation for working, just as her wages are. The employee is entitled to receive those benefits and to recover them if they are withheld without any particularized showing of detrimental reliance, just as she is entitled to recover the wages that were promised to her."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2010-09-804",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f38a7621a5795b00ac20400d6f5045f6f069881bcca71d1e8ead0beed0e85dca",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f38a7621a579-0002-0007",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 42,
        "start": 42
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: If this is a contract case, then where does the \"likely harm\" standard come from? If I'm owed something under a contract, I'm entitled to get that under the contract. I don't need to show that I was likely harmed by, that I relied in any -- in any way on anything."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2010-09-804",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f38a7621a5795b00ac20400d6f5045f6f069881bcca71d1e8ead0beed0e85dca",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f38a7621a579-0002-0009",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 56,
        "start": 56
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "(Whereupon, at 11:08 a.m., the case in the above-entitled matter was submitted.)"
    },
